+# Context for Codebase Quality Improvement Project
+
+## Overview
+You are helping improve the quality of a personal portfolio website codebase. A comprehensive quality assessment was performed (see CODEBASE_REPORT.md) which gave the codebase a Grade C+ and identified critical issues including security vulnerabilities, type safety problems, lack of testing, and other quality concerns.
+
+## Your Mission
+Follow the CODEBASE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md to systematically improve the codebase from Grade C+ to Grade A+ over 7 phases. Each phase addresses specific issues and must be completed on its own feature branch before merging to main.
+
+## Key Documents to Read First
+1. **CODEBASE_REPORT.md** - The quality assessment identifying all issues
+2. **CODEBASE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md** - The detailed plan with 7 phases
+3. **CLAUDE.md** - Project-specific instructions and guidelines
+
+## What to Do Next
+1. First, check the "Current Status Tracker" section at the bottom of CODEBASE_IMPROVEMENT_PLAN.md
+2. Identify the current phase and branch status
+3. Follow these rules:
+   - If status shows "⏸️ Pending Review" → Perform comprehensive review process
+   - If on main branch and phase incomplete → Create/checkout the phase branch
+   - If on phase branch → Continue implementing the phase tasks
+   - If review shows "❌ Review Failed" → Fix issues and review again
+   - If review shows "✅ Review Passed" → Merge to main and start next phase
+
+## Important Guidelines
+- **NEVER** merge without completing the comprehensive review process
+- Each phase has specific tasks that must ALL be completed
+- Follow the existing code patterns and conventions in CLAUDE.md
+- Run tests and linting after changes
+- Update the Current Status Tracker as you progress
+- If unsure about the current state, start by running:
+  ```bash
+  git status
+  git branch
+  git log --oneline -5
+  ```
+
+## Review Process Reminder
+Before ANY merge:
+1. Generate comprehensive diff report
+2. Verify ALL changes align with phase objectives
+3. Ensure no unintended modifications
+4. Confirm all tests pass
+5. Update status indicators
+
+## Expected Outcome
+By following this plan, we will systematically fix all critical issues and transform this into a world-class codebase worthy of a senior engineer's portfolio.
+
